plugins/mist - notices for the MIST package (mist.texture, mist.a64.rmp)

MIST's DSP is Beads', the texture synthesizer by Emilie Gillet: its granular processor (the four quality settings,
the delay mode, feedback, freeze), its reverb, limiters and wow and flutter, and the wavetable grains it plays when
nothing is patched in. MIST feeds it from a built-in oscillator at the trig's note (Plugin API 3 gives a machine no
audio input yet); mist_engine.h lists how it differs from Beads.
  Taken from:  https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack  commit f4cfa76 (2026-10-12; Beads' code in d8f4739)
               and its stmlib submodule, commit e3bd7c9
               by Emilie Gillet
  Licence:     MIT, Copyright 2016-2021 Emilie Gillet (LICENSE.beads; stmlib: third_party/eurorack/stmlib/LICENSE)
Beads' DSP files and the stmlib files it needs are vendored under third_party/eurorack, unchanged but for one
guarded change in beads/dsp/delay_line.h (third_party/eurorack/VENDORED.md lists the files and the change).

